{"id": "glm2_bracket_depth", "signature": "solve(s)", "statement": "Given a string s that may contain the bracket characters '(', ')', '<', '>' plus any other characters, first check whether every bracket in s is balanced and properly nested (other characters are ignored; the empty string is balanced). If the brackets are NOT balanced, return -1. If they are balanced, return the maximum bracket nesting depth (0 for the empty string or a string with no brackets).", "tests": [{"args": [""], "expected": 0}, {"args": ["<()>"], "expected": 2}, {"args": ["<<>>"], "expected": 2}, {"args": ["(<"], "expected": -1}, {"args": [")"], "expected": -1}, {"args": ["><"], "expected": -1}, {"args": ["a(b<c)d"], "expected": -1}, {"args": ["("], "expected": -1}, {"args": [")("], "expected": -1}, {"args": ["(("], "expected": -1}, {"args": ["<<>>()>"], "expected": -1}, {"args": ["()<>"], "expected": 1}, {"args": ["a"], "expected": 0}, {"args": ["<><"], "expected": -1}], "facts": [["arg", "s", "string"], ["iterate", "s"], ["ask", "balanced_brackets"], ["bracket_pair", "(", ")"], ["bracket_pair", "<", ">"], ["bracket_output", "max_depth"]], "deps": {"schema": ["bracket_match"], "uses": ["bracket_scan"], "solution_sha256": "e007a908bd807e9ba98f3f67caffb6569b66dee450b3ab11016dd1210e06a643", "reference_sha256": "658cc59697c8e5dbc614f8e4361959032095c42ddfd80a622b8a79af939bc20f"}}